.TH tapectl-cartridge-move 1  "tapectl-cartridge-move " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-cartridge\-move \- Move a cartridge to a location, taking its volumes with it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl cartridge move\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIBARCODE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move a cartridge to a location, taking its volumes with it
.PP
ADR\-0011: a cartridge\*(Aqs PLACE is a location, not a status. This moves `cartridges.location_id` and the `location_id` of every volume currently on the cartridge, in one transaction, so the shelf and the catalog cannot disagree. `volume move` does the same from the other end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Destination location name
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIBARCODE\fR>
Barcode
